{"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"title":"Sending batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport"],"anchor":"Sending-batches"},{"title":"Encoding a batch","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch"],"anchor":"Encoding-a-batch"},{"title":"Waiting between attempts","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/InvalidBackoff","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/NonPositiveRetry"],"anchor":"Waiting-between-attempts"},{"title":"Sending requests","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/URLSessionTransport","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransportError"],"anchor":"Sending-requests"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","title":"HTTPDestinations","modules":[{"name":"HTTPDestinations"}],"role":"collection","roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"HTTPDestinations"},"abstract":[{"text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination"},{"text":" is a destination that posts each batch it receives as one request. The body is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whatever its ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder"},{"text":" writes for the batch’s records, so events need no ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conformance and the wire format is yours. It sends with ","type":"text"},{"code":"URLSession","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" through","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/URLSessionTransport"},{"text":" by default, or through any ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport"},{"text":" you pass.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A send that gets no response, or a 5xx, 408 or 429 status, is sent again after the next wait of its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": 1 second, doubling up to 60 seconds, unless you pass another. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination takes the next batch only once this one is delivered or dropped, so a tracker’s store"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keeps the batch’s records until then. A batch the endpoint answers with any other status, whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"request can never be sent, or that the encoder can’t encode is dropped, logged and reported on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/dropReports","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" as an "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The tracing instrument injects the trace context of the batch’s first record into the request’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"header fields, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Content-Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is always the encoder’s.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reach for this module to send to a server whose format you write yourself. For TraffluentCollector’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"format, give the destination a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":"); for PostHog, a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PostHogBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PostHogEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":"). To read events inside the app or in a test, use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"InMemoryDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Destinations"},{"type":"text","text":") instead."}]},{"code":["import HTTPDestinations","","struct PlansEncoder: BatchEncoder {","    func encode(_ batch: [EventRecord]) -> EncodedBatch {","        let plans = batch.compactMap { ($0.event as? SignedUp)?.plan }","        return EncodedBatch(body: Data(plans.joined(separator: \"\\n\").utf8), contentType: \"text\/plain\")","    }","}","","let server = HTTPDestination(","    endpoint: endpointURL,","    headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(token)\"],","    encoder: PlansEncoder(),","    backoff: try ExponentialBackoff(initialDelay: .seconds(2), maximumDelay: .seconds(120)))","let drops = server.dropReports","let watching = Task {","    for await drop in drops {","        print(\"Dropped a batch: \\(drop)\")","    }","}","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: server)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","typ